<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Tangdao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1161">1161</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jin-song-wars">Jin–Song wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Tangdao was a naval battle fought off the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a> peninsula in late 1161, in which a small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Southern Song</a> fleet under Li Bao surprised and destroyed a much larger Jin fleet preparing to sail south. The Song used <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fire-arrow">fire arrows</a> and incendiary weapons against the anchored Jin ships. Together with the victory at Caishi later that month, it defeated the Jin emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wanyan-liang">Wanyan Liang</a>'s attempt to conquer the Song.</p></div>
